<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Constructing discrete probabilities from a relative frequency table</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A traffic enumerator at a busy junction in Mombasa records the number of heavy cargo trucks (\(X\)) that pass through during a 10-minute window. They collect data over many days and compile the frequency table below:</p>

<table style="width: 50%; text-align: center; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 20px;" border="1" cellpadding="5">
  <tbody>
    <tr style="background-color: #eceff1;">
      <td><b>Number of trucks (\(X\))</b></td>
      <td>0</td>
      <td>1</td>
      <td>2</td>
      <td>3</td>
      <td>4</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><b>Frequency (Days)</b></td>
      <td>{@f0@}</td>
      <td>{@f1@}</td>
      <td>{@f2@}</td>
      <td>{@f3@}</td>
      <td>{@f4@}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p><b>a) </b> Calculate the total number of 10-minute windows (days) recorded in this study.</p>
<p>\(\text{Total} =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> If a single 10-minute window is selected at random from the study, estimate the probability that <b>exactly 3 trucks</b> pass by.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> Estimate the probability that <b>strictly fewer than 3 trucks</b> pass during a randomly selected window.</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p><b>Part a: Total Observations</b><br>
The total number of recorded windows is the sum of all the frequencies in the table:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle \text{Total} = {@f0@} + {@f1@} + {@f2@} + {@f3@} + {@f4@} = {@ta1@} \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Relative Frequency</b><br>
To estimate the discrete probability, we convert the raw frequency into a relative frequency by dividing by the total number of observations:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X = 3) = \frac{\text{Frequency of } X=3}{\text{Total}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(X = 3) = \frac{{@f3@}}{{@ta1@}} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part c: Cumulative Probability</b><br>
The phrase "strictly fewer than 3" translates to the mathematical inequality \(X < 3\). This means we must include the outcomes for \(X = 0\), \(X = 1\), and \(X = 2\), but we <b>do not</b> include \(X = 3\).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X < 3) = P(X=0) + P(X=1) + P(X=2) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X < 3) = \frac{{@f0@}}{{@ta1@}} + \frac{{@f1@}}{{@ta1@}} + \frac{{@f2@}}{{@ta1@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(X < 3) = \frac{{@f0@} + {@f1@} + {@f2@}}{{@ta1@}} = \frac{{@f0 + f1 + f2@}}{{@ta1@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(X < 3) = {@ta3@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
